{"title":"Career Roadmap · Biochemist","role":"Biochemist","summary":"A Biochemist studies the chemical processes and molecular mechanisms underlying living systems. Biochemists work with proteins, enzymes, DNA/RNA, metabolites, cells and biological samples to understand biological processes and develop or test products.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science - General / Honours)","Course":"Biochemistry"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Biochemist studies the chemical processes and molecular mechanisms underlying living systems. Biochemists work with proteins, enzymes, DNA/RNA, metabolites, cells and biological samples to understand biological processes and develop or test products."},{"type":"p","text":"Career environments include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pharmaceutical R&D"},{"text":"Biotechnology"},{"text":"Diagnostics"},{"text":"Clinical laboratories"},{"text":"Food and nutrition"},{"text":"Academic research"},{"text":"Molecular biology"},{"text":"Drug discovery"},{"text":"Protein research"},{"text":"Industrial biotechnology"},{"text":"Quality control"},{"text":"Biomedical research"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Preparing and analyzing biological samples"},{"text":"Performing biochemical assays"},{"text":"Studying enzymes and proteins"},{"text":"DNA/RNA-related analysis"},{"text":"Spectrophotometric measurements"},{"text":"Chromatographic techniques"},{"text":"Cell and molecular biology workflows"},{"text":"Experimental design"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Scientific documentation"},{"text":"Research and product development"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Sc graduate, entry-level roles are often Laboratory Analyst, Research Assistant, QC Analyst, Biochemistry Technician or Junior Research Associate. More independent biochemist/scientist roles